--- ts:docs/port/TS_PORT_DECISIONS.md D-016(5) / D-033 lines @ cb1cbcb2e88b898e8c081b0abbfabc1630079c00
165:  5. [Replace Python-specific tool with TypeScript equivalent] Spinner/progress during network fetch (rich.Progress replacement) → yocto-spinner on stderr (its default), additionally gated on process.stderr.isTTY and CI env
174:  5. Stderr-by-default satisfies cli-standards R7.1 (progress=diagnostics) and fixes the source wart where progress text polluted stdout; chosen over ora to avoid a chalk+picocolors double color stack. [https://github.com/sindresorhus/yocto-spinner (stderr default, 1.2.1 2026-07-06); https://github.com/sindresorhus/ora (stderr default but chalk dep)]
356:- Decision: (1) styleText, wrapped in src/lib/colors.ts. Supersedes D-016(3); D-016's yocto-spinner rationale re-grounded on zero-dep consistency rather than avoiding a picocolors double-stack; T06's runtime-dep list drops to 5.
398:- Decision: (1) Exit 130 on prompt interrupt/stdin-close, clean message, no leaked library internals — a deliberate, documented deviation from the source's swallow-to-0. Same rework also: implements D-018(4)'s outstanding machine-mode error envelope ({"error":{code,message}} single JSON object on stderr when --format json) and a --json alias for --format json; records parity rows for the added 30s request timeout and the positive---limit tightening; guards the spinner against 0-column TTYs.

